# PAM policy for sg-keyring (the sign-in notice's "saved passwords"): it
# checks, as the person and in their session, that the password they typed is
# their current sign-in password before their keyring is re-encrypted with it
# -- a typing slip there would lock the keyring away again. Only the password
# check: pam_unix, unprivileged, asks unix_chkpwd, which answers for one's own
# account alone.
@include common-auth
